<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28621" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Memphis</span></b> , is and ĭdos,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεμφις</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Middle
				Egypt, celebrated as the residence of the Egyptian kings</i>,
			now <i>Metrahenny</i> (fourteen miles south of Cairo),
				<i><span class="en">Mel.
				1, 9, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 85, 87, § 201</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">5, 9, 9, §
			50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 45, 11 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3,
				26, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 4, 84</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 3,
				11, 34</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quae colis, et Memphin, palmiferamque Pharon,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 2, 13, 7</span></i>
			.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Memphītes</span></b> ,
			ae, m.
			<i>adj., Memphite, of</i> or <i>from the
				city of Memphis, Egyptian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Memphiten plangere bovem,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Apis</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tib. 1,
					8</span></i>
			 (7), 28 lapis, <i><span class="en">Plin. 36, 7, 11, §
			56</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Memphītĭcus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., Memphitic, Egyptian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">templa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 1, 77</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ensis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					10, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Memphītis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f.
			<i>adj., Memphite, Egyptian</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terrā Memphitide,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					15, 122</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vacca,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Io</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 3, 393</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cymba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					4, 136</span></i>
			. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
